# #103 companion: `exit of N` unwinds via g_has_error + g_exit_requested.
# The old aot_call_name ignored both flags — the program RAN PAST the exit
# (printed "never", exited 0). Now the AOT honors the requested code, so
# both sides die with rc 3 and identical prior stdout. Rides the _err class
# for its both-die + death-code-equality contract (nothing raises here).
print of "one"
exit of 3
print of "never"
